WEBVTT

00:00:00.656 --> 00:00:06.925
From the approved test, create an invoice linked to the customer, location, and test.

00:00:06.925 --> 00:00:12.149
Confirm the service description, price, issue date, and due date.

00:00:12.149 --> 00:00:16.662
This link lets the submission workflow check payment eligibility.

00:00:31.048 --> 00:00:35.290
Save the draft and review its amount and related test.

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:38.777
A draft is editable and has not been issued.

00:00:38.777 --> 00:00:47.317
An unpaid linked invoice can hold municipality submission until payment is recorded or an authorized office override is approved.

00:01:01.308 --> 00:01:04.524
Issue the invoice for manual delivery.

00:01:04.524 --> 00:01:08.787
This locks the issued document and enables payment recording.

00:01:08.787 --> 00:01:16.195
The application records an issued status; this recording does not email the invoice or run an online checkout.

00:01:31.663 --> 00:01:35.194
Record the fictional check payment and reference.

00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:40.076
The saved invoice balance becomes zero and status becomes paid.

00:01:40.076 --> 00:01:47.194
Manual recording does not move money through Stripe; it documents a payment you have already received and verified.
